Third-party components
----------------------

The engine statically links third-party libraries. THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES,
published beside each binary, covers them.

That file is not a straight copy of MongoDB's own. Theirs describes what they
distribute, and this library links a different set: it drops the components a
server needs and no embedded engine does, and it reaches a few their release
binaries never carry. So the file is assembled from the Bazel link command
itself, which lists every object that went in, and the build fails if any
linked component is unaccounted for. scripts/third-party-dispositions.tsv
records how each one is covered, and scripts/collect-third-party-notices
enforces it.
